            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Italian for to browse, then the Italian for the link."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: pubblicare",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "pubblicare — \"to publish, to post\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Se pubblichi la foto, tutti la vedono. If you post the photo, everyone sees it."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "For books too: pubblicare un romanzo."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "pubblicare is a learned borrowing from Latin pūblicāre \"to make public\" (Lewis & Short), from pūblicus \"of the people, public\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling, explaining and describing at B1."
